*Readme file for How Government Reactions to Violence Worsen Social Welfare: Evidence from Peru
Sexton, Wellhausen and Findley     *
*********************************************************************************************************************

The following files can be used to replicate the results in the manuscript and appendix employing Stata and R.


***********************************************
* STATA FILES
***********************************************


The primary replication file is “0_SWF_replication.do,” created in Stata 13. Provided all the files are in the same directory they will run from this do file automatically. 

The 0_SWF_replication.do  file accesses the following data sets:

(1) swf-peru-ajps.dta:  Main data panel
(2) debate_attacks.dta: Data on Peruvian Congressional debates
(3) attacks_list.dta: Information on attacks by month
(4) hurdle.dta: Data for the hurdle model in the appendix


We include the source files for a user-created command “brl” that is employed in 0_SWF_replication.do:

brl.ado
brl.hlp
brl.pkg

The .do file includes instructions for installing the brl package.

 
***********************************************
* R FILES
***********************************************

For the Non-parametric Combination (NPC) implementation in the appendix, we include R code and data.

(1) SWF-NPC-implementation.R: code that implements the NPC
(2) swf-peru-ajps_forR.dta: input data 

***************
*CODEBOOK FILE*
***************
“CODEBOOK.pdf": codebook of all variables used in the analyses 


